    "notes": [
        "Mathematics onDefault contrast (4.32:1) is below the 4.5:1 AA threshold for normal text. Suitable for large/bold text, icons, and badges (3:1 threshold) but avoid using the Mathematics key color as a fill behind small body text.",
        "role.light.primary and role.dark.primary were changed from a fixed {color.key.primary} reference to {color.palette.primary.40} / {color.palette.primary.80}, matching the secondary/tertiary pattern. The exact brand hex (#4D5DFB) is preserved separately as brand.primary.",
        "Neutral tones 4, 6, 12, 17, 22, 24 were missing from the Matisse export but referenced by dark-mode surface roles. These were generated by interpolation, preserving the 231 deg hue and matching the saturation/lightness curve of the surrounding tones.",
        "role.dark.error/onError/errorContainer/onErrorContainer referenced 'color.palette.error' (lowercase) but the palette key is 'Error' (capitalized) -- fixed to resolve correctly."
    ]
